    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0365" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.85/40</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-07T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1918,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s [telegram of July 20, answering your] 42. British Ministry of
                    Shipping has informed our Embassy at London that steamers <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tobolsk</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Indighirka</hi>
                    are not being held at Hong Kong, but are employed in important services from
                    which they can not be spared.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
